i) In developing the proposed amendments, evaluate appropriate standards related to apiary location, setbacks, hive density, parcel size, registration, water supply, fire safety, nuisance prevention, and the protection of neighboring properties and public rights-of-way;

1) Develop recommendations that recognize the agricultural and community benefits of managed honeybees while protecting native pollinators and sensitive habitats, including consideration of native pollinator habitat, native plantings, location-appropriate hive densities, and additional safeguards near ecologically sensitive areas;

b) Direct Agricultural Commissioner staff to consult with local beekeepers, agricultural producers, native-pollinator or other interested stakeholders in developing the proposed amendments;

